/*
 * M1, slice 1: two members, one Update commit (RFC 9420)
 *
 * Scope:  everything in M0, then B commits an update of its own leaf with a
 *         path and A processes it (epoch 2). Members now hold state and the
 *         adversary can reveal it. Decisions D1-D4 and simplifications S1-S9
 *         of m0.spthy carry over unchanged.
 *         Not yet: a third member, Remove, an Update proposal committed by
 *         someone else, A as committer, repeated commits.
 * Status: results are whatever `make` records in results/m1.txt.
 *         Section numbers refer to RFC 9420.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * DECISIONS NEW IN M1
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * E1  State per member per epoch (9.2): init_secret, encryption_secret and
 *     the member's leaf private key. epoch_secret, joiner_secret and
 *     commit_secret are not kept; 9.2 requires them deleted once consumed.
 *     encryption_secret stands for all message keys of the epoch and is the
 *     "group key" in the lemmas (action GroupKey).
 * E2  A member deletes an epoch's state when it moves to the next epoch
 *     (restriction state_deleted_on_leaving), so RevState is only possible
 *     while the member is in that epoch. RevState does not reveal the
 *     signature key (that is RevSig). A's epoch-0 state cannot be revealed.
 * E3  Only B (leaf 1) commits and only A (leaf 0) processes. The mirrored
 *     pair of rules is not written, so results about "the committer" and
 *     "the other member" hold for this one assignment.
 * E4  The update is an empty Commit with a path (12.4). B replaces its leaf
 *     key and sends one fresh path secret, sealed to A's leaf key with the
 *     provisional GroupContext as context (7.6). With two leaves this is the
 *     whole UpdatePath, except that the root key pair derived from the path
 *     secret is not kept: with two members nobody encrypts to it.
 *     commit_secret = expand(path_secret, 'path', 'empty').
 * E5  The Commit is sent as content, signature and confirmation tag, with no
 *     membership_tag (6.2) and no PrivateMessage encryption. The adversary
 *     is stronger than in the RFC: forging a commit needs the sender's
 *     signature key and the confirmation tag, but no membership key.
 * E6  The transcript chain continues (8.2):
 *     interim1 = h(<cth1, tag1>),  cth2 = h(<interim1, content, csig>).
 * E7  Epochs are the constants '0', '1', '2'. No rule can repeat, so no
 *     induction is needed. Revisit when commits can repeat.
 * E8  B moves to epoch 2 as soon as it commits (as S6 in M0).
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * STATE FACTS NEW IN M1
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * StA1($A, gid, GC1, interim1, init1, ~lk, leafA, leafB)
 * StB1($B, gid, GC1, interim1, init1, ~lk, leafB, leafA)
 *                          Linear. What each member needs to leave epoch 1.
 * !Secrets($X, gid, ep, init, enc, lk)
 *                          Read only by RevState (E1, E2).
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * KEY SCHEDULE, epoch 2  (8)
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *   init1 = expand(es1, 'init', 'empty')
 *   enc1  = expand(es1, 'encryption', 'empty')
 *   tree2 = <leafA, leafB2>          leafB2 = <$B, hpk(~lk2), pk(~sigB)>
 *   prov  = <gid, '2', h(tree2), cth1>              provisional GroupContext
 *   ct    = hseal(lkA, <'UpdatePathNode', prov>, ~ps)
 *   content = <gid, '1', $B, 'commit', <'path', leafB2, ct>>
 *   csig  = sign(<'FramedContentTBS', content, GC1>, ~sigB)
 *   cth2  = h(<interim1, content, csig>)
 *   GC2   = <gid, '2', h(tree2), cth2>
 *   cs    = expand(~ps, 'path', 'empty')                      commit_secret
 *   js2   = expand(extract(init1, cs), 'joiner', GC2)
 *   es2   = expand(extract(js2, 'zero'), 'epoch', GC2)
 *   tag2  = mac(expand(es2, 'confirm', 'empty'), cth2)
 *   Commit on the wire: <content, csig, tag2>
 *   A accepts if csig verifies under the key in B's current leaf, the new
 *   leaf key differs from the old one (12.4.2), ct opens under A's leaf key,
 *   and the tag recomputed from its own init1 equals tag2.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * ADVERSARY
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * As M0 (Dolev-Yao, RevSig, RevInit), plus:
 *   RevState(X, gid, ep)   init_secret, encryption_secret and leaf private
 *                          key that X holds for that epoch of that group.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * LEMMAS NEW IN M1
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * exec_update        The honest run reaches epoch 2 with both members
 *                    agreeing, with no reveal.
 * agreement_update   If A processes a commit from B, B made that commit with
 *                    the same GroupContext and epoch secret, unless A's or
 *                    B's signature key leaked first.
 * fs_epoch1          Forward secrecy. The epoch-1 group key stays secret even
 *                    if any state is revealed in epoch 2. Excuses: a state
 *                    reveal in epoch 1, or any RevSig or RevInit.
 * pcs_epoch2         Post-compromise security. After B's commit the epoch-2
 *                    group key is secret even if B's own epoch-1 state had
 *                    been revealed. Excuses: a state reveal in epoch 2, a
 *                    reveal of the other member's epoch-1 state, or any
 *                    RevSig or RevInit.
 * control_state_reveal
 *                    exists-trace. One epoch-1 state reveal is enough to
 *                    learn the epoch-1 group key.
 * attack_no_pcs_when_peer_compromised
 *                    exists-trace. If A's epoch-1 state was revealed and B
 *                    then commits, the adversary knows both secret inputs of
 *                    epoch 2's key schedule (init_secret of epoch 1 and the
 *                    path secret): only the committer heals. The lemma is
 *                    stated on the inputs because that is cheap to prove.
 *                    The same attack on the group key itself is at the end
 *                    of the file, commented out: Tamarin finds the trace but
 *                    needs about 10 minutes and 6 GB.
 *
 * Tool note: the rules are large enough that Tamarin's derivation checks
 * time out at the default 5 seconds. Run with --derivcheck-timeout=120.
 */

theory M1
begin

builtins: hashing, signing

functions: hpk/1, hseal/3, hopen/3, extract/2, expand/3, mac/2
equations: hopen(sk, info, hseal(hpk(sk), info, m)) = m

restriction Eq:
  "All x y #i. Eq(x, y) @ i ==> x = y"

restriction Neq:
  "All x #i. Neq(x, x) @ i ==> F"

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Setup
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* Authentication Service (D4): binds one long-term signature key to X. */
rule Register_sig:
  [ Fr(~sig) ]
  --[ Register($X, pk(~sig)) ]->
  [ !Ltk($X, ~sig), !Cred($X, pk(~sig)), Out(pk(~sig)) ]

restriction one_key_per_identity:
  "All X pk1 pk2 #i #j.
     Register(X, pk1) @ i & Register(X, pk2) @ j ==> #i = #j"

/* B publishes a KeyPackage (10) and keeps the private keys behind it. */
rule Publish_KeyPackage:
  let leaf = <$B, hpk(~lk), pk(~sig)>
      kp   = <hpk(~init), leaf>
  in
  [ !Ltk($B, ~sig), Fr(~init), Fr(~lk) ]
  --[ PublishedKP($B, kp) ]->
  [ KeyPkg($B, ~init, ~lk), !InitKey($B, ~init, kp)
  , Out(<kp, sign(<'KeyPackageTBS', kp>, ~sig)>) ]

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Protocol
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* A creates a one-member group at epoch 0 (11). Nothing is sent. */
rule Create_Group:
  [ !Ltk($A, ~sig), Fr(~gid), Fr(~lk), Fr(~es0) ]
  --[ Created($A, ~gid) ]->
  [ Group0($A, ~gid, ~lk, ~es0) ]

/* A commits an Add of B with no path (D1) and sends the Welcome (12.4.1,
   12.4.3.1). A takes the KeyPackage from the network and checks its
   signature against the AS binding for the identity in its leaf. */
rule Commit_Add:
  let leafA    = <$A, hpk(~lk), pk(~sigA)>
      leafB    = <$B, lkB, pkB>
      kp       = <ik, leafB>
      GC0      = <~gid, '0', h(leafA), 'empty'>
      init0    = expand(~es0, 'init', 'empty')
      ck0      = expand(~es0, 'confirm', 'empty')
      tag0     = mac(ck0, 'empty')
      interim0 = h(<'empty', tag0>)
      content  = <~gid, '0', $A, 'commit', <'add', kp>>
      csig     = sign(<'FramedContentTBS', content, GC0>, ~sigA)
      tree1    = <leafA, leafB>
      cth1     = h(<interim0, content, csig>)
      GC1      = <~gid, '1', h(tree1), cth1>
      js       = expand(extract(init0, 'zero'), 'joiner', GC1)
      es1      = expand(extract(js, 'zero'), 'epoch', GC1)
      ck1      = expand(es1, 'confirm', 'empty')
      tag1     = mac(ck1, cth1)
      gi       = <GC1, tag1>
      gisig    = sign(<'GroupInfoTBS', gi>, ~sigA)
      info     = <gi, gisig, tree1>
      egs      = hseal(ik, <'Welcome', info>, js)
      interim1 = h(<cth1, tag1>)
      init1    = expand(es1, 'init', 'empty')
      enc1     = expand(es1, 'encryption', 'empty')
  in
  [ Group0($A, ~gid, ~lk, ~es0), !Ltk($A, ~sigA)
  , !Cred($B, pkB), In(<kp, kpsig>) ]
  --[ Eq(verify(kpsig, <'KeyPackageTBS', kp>, pkB), true)
    , Neq($A, $B)                                                  /* S8 */
    , Committed($A, ~gid, $B, kp, GC1, es1)
    , GroupKey($A, ~gid, '1', enc1) ]->
  [ StA1($A, ~gid, GC1, interim1, init1, ~lk, leafA, leafB)
  , !Secrets($A, ~gid, '1', init1, enc1, ~lk)
  , Out(<h(<'KeyPackageRef', kp>), egs, info>) ]

/* B joins from a Welcome (12.4.3.1). Opening egs is done by pattern
   matching on hseal under B's own init key. */
rule Join:
  let leafB = <$B, hpk(~lk), pk(~sigB)>
      kp    = <hpk(~init), leafB>
      leafA = <$A, lkA, pkA>
      tree1 = <leafA, leafB>
      GC1   = <gid, '1', h(tree1), cth1>
      gi    = <GC1, tag1>
      info  = <gi, gisig, tree1>
      egs   = hseal(hpk(~init), <'Welcome', info>, js)
      es1   = expand(extract(js, 'zero'), 'epoch', GC1)
      ck1   = expand(es1, 'confirm', 'empty')
      interim1 = h(<cth1, tag1>)
      init1 = expand(es1, 'init', 'empty')
      enc1  = expand(es1, 'encryption', 'empty')
  in
  [ KeyPkg($B, ~init, ~lk), !Ltk($B, ~sigB)
  , !Cred($A, pkA), In(<h(<'KeyPackageRef', kp>), egs, info>) ]
  --[ Eq(verify(gisig, <'GroupInfoTBS', gi>, pkA), true)
    , Eq(tag1, mac(ck1, cth1))
    , Joined($B, gid, $A, kp, GC1, es1)
    , GroupKey($B, gid, '1', enc1) ]->
  [ StB1($B, gid, GC1, interim1, init1, ~lk, leafB, leafA)
  , !Secrets($B, gid, '1', init1, enc1, ~lk) ]


/* B (leaf 1) commits an update of its own leaf with a path (12.4, 7.4-7.6).
   In a two-leaf tree the path is one secret, sealed to A's leaf key. */
rule Commit_Update:
  let leafB   = <$B, hpk(~lk), pk(~sigB)>
      leafA   = <$A, lkA, pkA>
      GC1     = <gid, '1', th1, cth1>
      leafB2  = <$B, hpk(~lk2), pk(~sigB)>
      tree2   = <leafA, leafB2>
      prov    = <gid, '2', h(tree2), cth1>
      ct      = hseal(lkA, <'UpdatePathNode', prov>, ~ps)
      content = <gid, '1', $B, 'commit', <'path', leafB2, ct>>
      csig    = sign(<'FramedContentTBS', content, GC1>, ~sigB)
      cth2    = h(<interim1, content, csig>)
      GC2     = <gid, '2', h(tree2), cth2>
      cs      = expand(~ps, 'path', 'empty')
      js2     = expand(extract(init1, cs), 'joiner', GC2)
      es2     = expand(extract(js2, 'zero'), 'epoch', GC2)
      ck2     = expand(es2, 'confirm', 'empty')
      tag2    = mac(ck2, cth2)
      init2   = expand(es2, 'init', 'empty')
      enc2    = expand(es2, 'encryption', 'empty')
  in
  [ StB1($B, gid, GC1, interim1, init1, ~lk, leafB, leafA)
  , !Ltk($B, ~sigB), Fr(~lk2), Fr(~ps) ]
  --[ Left($B, gid, '1')
    , Updated($B, gid, GC2, es2)
    , SecretInputs($B, gid, init1, ~ps)
    , GroupKey($B, gid, '2', enc2) ]->
  [ !Secrets($B, gid, '2', init2, enc2, ~lk2)
  , Out(<content, csig, tag2>) ]

/* A (leaf 0) processes B's commit (12.4.2). */
rule Process_Update:
  let leafA   = <$A, hpk(~lk), pkA>
      leafB   = <$B, lkB, pkB>
      GC1     = <gid, '1', th1, cth1>
      leafB2  = <$B, lkB2, pkB>
      tree2   = <leafA, leafB2>
      prov    = <gid, '2', h(tree2), cth1>
      ct      = hseal(hpk(~lk), <'UpdatePathNode', prov>, ps)
      content = <gid, '1', $B, 'commit', <'path', leafB2, ct>>
      cth2    = h(<interim1, content, csig>)
      GC2     = <gid, '2', h(tree2), cth2>
      cs      = expand(ps, 'path', 'empty')
      js2     = expand(extract(init1, cs), 'joiner', GC2)
      es2     = expand(extract(js2, 'zero'), 'epoch', GC2)
      ck2     = expand(es2, 'confirm', 'empty')
      init2   = expand(es2, 'init', 'empty')
      enc2    = expand(es2, 'encryption', 'empty')
  in
  [ StA1($A, gid, GC1, interim1, init1, ~lk, leafA, leafB)
  , In(<content, csig, tag2>) ]
  --[ Eq(verify(csig, <'FramedContentTBS', content, GC1>, pkB), true)
    , Eq(tag2, mac(ck2, cth2))
    , Neq(lkB, lkB2)
    , Left($A, gid, '1')
    , Processed($A, gid, $B, GC2, es2)
    , GroupKey($A, gid, '2', enc2) ]->
  [ !Secrets($A, gid, '2', init2, enc2, ~lk) ]

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Adversary
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */

rule RevSig:
  [ !Ltk($X, ~sig) ]
  --[ RevSig($X) ]->
  [ Out(~sig) ]

/* Reveals the init key behind a KeyPackage. Only possible before B joins
   with it: B deletes the key on joining (S5). */
rule RevInit:
  [ !InitKey($B, ~init, kp) ]
  --[ RevInit($B, kp) ]->
  [ Out(~init) ]

/* Reveals what member X holds for one epoch of one group (9.2): the init
   secret, the message-protection secret and X's leaf private key. Only
   possible while X is in that epoch. */
rule RevState:
  [ !Secrets($X, gid, ep, init, enc, lk) ]
  --[ RevState($X, gid, ep) ]->
  [ Out(<init, enc, lk>) ]

restriction state_deleted_on_leaving:
  "All X gid ep #r #t.
     RevState(X, gid, ep) @ r & Left(X, gid, ep) @ t ==> r < t"

restriction init_key_deleted_on_join:
  "All B gid A kp GC es #i #r.
     Joined(B, gid, A, kp, GC, es) @ i & RevInit(B, kp) @ r ==> r < i"

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * M0 lemmas, unchanged, as regression tests
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */

lemma exec: exists-trace
  "Ex A B gid kp GC es #i #j.
       Committed(A, gid, B, kp, GC, es) @ i
     & Joined(B, gid, A, kp, GC, es) @ j
     & not (Ex X #r. RevSig(X) @ r)
     & not (Ex X k #r. RevInit(X, k) @ r)
     /* one of each step, to keep the search small */
     & (All X1 X2 g1 g2 #a #b.
          Created(X1, g1) @ a & Created(X2, g2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All X1 X2 k1 k2 #a #b.
          PublishedKP(X1, k1) @ a & PublishedKP(X2, k2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All A1 A2 g1 g2 B1 B2 k1 k2 c1 c2 e1 e2 #a #b.
            Committed(A1, g1, B1, k1, c1, e1) @ a
          & Committed(A2, g2, B2, k2, c2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)"

lemma join_once:
  "All B kp gid1 gid2 A1 A2 GC1 GC2 es1 es2 #i #j.
       Joined(B, gid1, A1, kp, GC1, es1) @ i
     & Joined(B, gid2, A2, kp, GC2, es2) @ j
     ==> #i = #j"

lemma secrecy_committer [reuse]:
  "All A gid B kp GC es #i.
     Committed(A, gid, B, kp, GC, es) @ i
     ==> not (Ex #k. K(es) @ k)
       | (Ex #r. RevSig(B) @ r & r < i)
       | (Ex #r. RevInit(B, kp) @ r)"

lemma agreement_state [reuse]:
  "All B gid A kp GC es #i.
       Joined(B, gid, A, kp, GC, es) @ i
     ==> (Ex B2 kp2 #j. Committed(A, gid, B2, kp2, GC, es) @ j & j < i)
       | (Ex #r. RevSig(A) @ r & r < i)"

lemma secrecy_joiner:
  "All B gid A kp GC es #i.
     Joined(B, gid, A, kp, GC, es) @ i
     ==> not (Ex #k. K(es) @ k)
       | (Ex #r. RevSig(A) @ r & r < i)
       | (Ex #r. RevSig(B) @ r & r < i)
       | (Ex #r. RevInit(B, kp) @ r)"

lemma agreement_keypackage:
  "All B gid A kp GC es #i.
       Joined(B, gid, A, kp, GC, es) @ i
     ==> (Ex #j. Committed(A, gid, B, kp, GC, es) @ j & j < i)
       | (Ex #r. RevSig(A) @ r & r < i)
       | (Ex #r. RevSig(B) @ r & r < i)"

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Attack lemmas (exists-trace). "verified" means Tamarin found the trace.
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */

lemma attack_joiner_secrecy_needs_own_key: exists-trace
  "Ex B gid A kp GC es #i #k.
       Joined(B, gid, A, kp, GC, es) @ i & K(es) @ k
     & not (Ex #r. RevSig(A) @ r)
     & not (Ex X k2 #r. RevInit(X, k2) @ r)
     & (All X1 X2 g1 g2 #a #b.
          Created(X1, g1) @ a & Created(X2, g2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All X1 X2 k1 k2 #a #b.
          PublishedKP(X1, k1) @ a & PublishedKP(X2, k2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All A1 A2 g1 g2 B1 B2 k1 k2 c1 c2 e1 e2 #a #b.
            Committed(A1, g1, B1, k1, c1, e1) @ a
          & Committed(A2, g2, B2, k2, c2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)"

lemma attack_keypackage_agreement_needs_own_key: exists-trace
  "Ex B gid A kp GC es #i.
       Joined(B, gid, A, kp, GC, es) @ i
     & not (Ex #j. Committed(A, gid, B, kp, GC, es) @ j)
     & not (Ex #r. RevSig(A) @ r)
     & not (Ex X k2 #r. RevInit(X, k2) @ r)
     & (All X1 X2 g1 g2 #a #b.
          Created(X1, g1) @ a & Created(X2, g2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All X1 X2 k1 k2 #a #b.
          PublishedKP(X1, k1) @ a & PublishedKP(X2, k2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All A1 A2 g1 g2 B1 B2 k1 k2 c1 c2 e1 e2 #a #b.
            Committed(A1, g1, B1, k1, c1, e1) @ a
          & Committed(A2, g2, B2, k2, c2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)"

lemma control_forged_welcome: exists-trace
  "Ex B gid A kp GC es #i.
       Joined(B, gid, A, kp, GC, es) @ i
     & not (Ex A2 g2 B2 k2 c2 e2 #j. Committed(A2, g2, B2, k2, c2, e2) @ j)
     & (All X1 X2 k1 k2 #a #b.
          PublishedKP(X1, k1) @ a & PublishedKP(X2, k2) @ b ==> #a = #b)"

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * M1 lemmas
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */

lemma exec_update: exists-trace
  "Ex A B gid kp GC1 es1 GC2 es2 #i #j #u #p.
       Committed(A, gid, B, kp, GC1, es1) @ i
     & Joined(B, gid, A, kp, GC1, es1) @ j
     & Updated(B, gid, GC2, es2) @ u
     & Processed(A, gid, B, GC2, es2) @ p
     & not (Ex X #r. RevSig(X) @ r)
     & not (Ex X k #r. RevInit(X, k) @ r)
     & not (Ex X g e #r. RevState(X, g, e) @ r)
     & (All X1 X2 g1 g2 #a #b.
          Created(X1, g1) @ a & Created(X2, g2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All X1 X2 k1 k2 #a #b.
          PublishedKP(X1, k1) @ a & PublishedKP(X2, k2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All A1 A2 g1 g2 B1 B2 k1 k2 c1 c2 e1 e2 #a #b.
            Committed(A1, g1, B1, k1, c1, e1) @ a
          & Committed(A2, g2, B2, k2, c2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All X1 X2 g1 g2 c1 c2 e1 e2 #a #b.
            Updated(X1, g1, c1, e1) @ a
          & Updated(X2, g2, c2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)"

lemma agreement_update [reuse]:
  "All A gid B GC es #i.
       Processed(A, gid, B, GC, es) @ i
     ==> (Ex #j. Updated(B, gid, GC, es) @ j & j < i)
       | (Ex #r. RevSig(B) @ r & r < i)
       | (Ex #r. RevSig(A) @ r & r < i)"

lemma fs_epoch1:
  "All X gid k #i.
     GroupKey(X, gid, '1', k) @ i
     ==> not (Ex #j. K(k) @ j)
       | (Ex Y #r. RevState(Y, gid, '1') @ r)
       | (Ex Y #r. RevSig(Y) @ r)
       | (Ex Y kp #r. RevInit(Y, kp) @ r)"

lemma pcs_epoch2:
  "All X gid k B GC es #i #u.
       GroupKey(X, gid, '2', k) @ i & Updated(B, gid, GC, es) @ u
     ==> not (Ex #j. K(k) @ j)
       | (Ex Y #r. RevState(Y, gid, '2') @ r)
       | (Ex Y #r. RevState(Y, gid, '1') @ r & not (Y = B))
       | (Ex Y #r. RevSig(Y) @ r)
       | (Ex Y kp #r. RevInit(Y, kp) @ r)"

lemma control_state_reveal: exists-trace
  "Ex X Y gid k #i #j #r.
       GroupKey(X, gid, '1', k) @ i & K(k) @ j
     & RevState(Y, gid, '1') @ r
     & (All Y1 Y2 g1 g2 e1 e2 #a #b.
          RevState(Y1, g1, e1) @ a & RevState(Y2, g2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & not (Ex Z #s. RevSig(Z) @ s)
     & not (Ex Z k2 #s. RevInit(Z, k2) @ s)
     & (All X1 X2 g1 g2 #a #b.
          Created(X1, g1) @ a & Created(X2, g2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All X1 X2 k1 k2 #a #b.
          PublishedKP(X1, k1) @ a & PublishedKP(X2, k2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All A1 A2 g1 g2 B1 B2 k1 k2 c1 c2 e1 e2 #a #b.
            Committed(A1, g1, B1, k1, c1, e1) @ a
          & Committed(A2, g2, B2, k2, c2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All X1 X2 g1 g2 c1 c2 e1 e2 #a #b.
            Updated(X1, g1, c1, e1) @ a
          & Updated(X2, g2, c2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)"

/* No healing when the other member was the compromised one. A's epoch-1
   state is revealed, B then commits, and the adversary knows both secret
   inputs of epoch 2's key schedule: init_secret of epoch 1 and the path
   secret. Stated on the inputs because that derivation is short. */
lemma attack_no_pcs_when_peer_compromised: exists-trace
  "Ex A B gid GC es i1 ps #u #p #r #x #y.
       Updated(B, gid, GC, es) @ u
     & SecretInputs(B, gid, i1, ps) @ u
     & Processed(A, gid, B, GC, es) @ p
     & RevState(A, gid, '1') @ r & r < u
     & K(i1) @ x & K(ps) @ y
     & (All Y1 Y2 g1 g2 e1 e2 #a #b.
          RevState(Y1, g1, e1) @ a & RevState(Y2, g2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & not (Ex X #s. RevSig(X) @ s)
     & not (Ex X k2 #s. RevInit(X, k2) @ s)
     & (All X1 X2 g1 g2 #a #b.
          Created(X1, g1) @ a & Created(X2, g2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All X1 X2 k1 k2 #a #b.
          PublishedKP(X1, k1) @ a & PublishedKP(X2, k2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All A1 A2 g1 g2 B1 B2 k1 k2 c1 c2 e1 e2 #a #b.
            Committed(A1, g1, B1, k1, c1, e1) @ a
          & Committed(A2, g2, B2, k2, c2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
     & (All X1 X2 g1 g2 c1 c2 e1 e2 #a #b.
            Updated(X1, g1, c1, e1) @ a
          & Updated(X2, g2, c2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)"

/* The same attack stated on the epoch-2 group key itself. Tamarin 1.12.0
   finds the trace (39 steps) but took about 10 minutes and 6 GB on a 2-core
   machine, so it is left out of the default run. Unlike the lemma above it
   does not require the reveal to come before B's commit, only before A
   leaves epoch 1. Remove the comment markers to run it.

  lemma attack_no_pcs_group_key: exists-trace
    "Ex A B gid GC es k #u #p #i #j #r.
         Updated(B, gid, GC, es) @ u
       & Processed(A, gid, B, GC, es) @ p
       & GroupKey(B, gid, '2', k) @ i & K(k) @ j
       & RevState(A, gid, '1') @ r
       & (All Y1 Y2 g1 g2 e1 e2 #a #b.
            RevState(Y1, g1, e1) @ a & RevState(Y2, g2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
       & not (Ex X #s. RevSig(X) @ s)
       & not (Ex X k2 #s. RevInit(X, k2) @ s)
       & (All X1 X2 g1 g2 #a #b.
            Created(X1, g1) @ a & Created(X2, g2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
       & (All X1 X2 k1 k2 #a #b.
            PublishedKP(X1, k1) @ a & PublishedKP(X2, k2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
       & (All A1 A2 g1 g2 B1 B2 k1 k2 c1 c2 e1 e2 #a #b.
              Committed(A1, g1, B1, k1, c1, e1) @ a
            & Committed(A2, g2, B2, k2, c2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)
       & (All X1 X2 g1 g2 c1 c2 e1 e2 #a #b.
              Updated(X1, g1, c1, e1) @ a
            & Updated(X2, g2, c2, e2) @ b ==> #a = #b)"
*/

end
